# gjalla

The same way you wouldn't try to memorize every code diff and instead
use git, you wouldn't try to memorize every system design detail,
architecture decision, or functional intent across sessions. You use
gjalla.

gjalla is your persistent memory and traceability layer for everything
above the code: what the system is, what it should be, what changed,
and why. It survives session boundaries, works across teammates and
tools, and means you never start from zero.

This helps you and your human collaborators manage both the
expectations and the reality of the system as a whole. When you use
gjalla, you're the dream team.

What that gives you:
- Architecture, rules, capabilities, data flows, and tech stack are
  queryable — not re-derived from code every session
- Memories persist what you learn; change history tracks what was done
  and by whom
- Constraints are machine-readable — check them before committing
- Impact analysis shows blast radius before changes land
- Specs scaffold with architectural context already filled in

## Getting started

```
pip install gjalla
gjalla auth login
gjalla setup
```

`gjalla setup` installs detailed instructions and workflows locally.

## Key tools

| Tool | Use when... |
|------|-------------|
| get_architecture_spec | Load the master spec — containers, components, relationships |
| get_architecture_element_details | Drill into a specific element |
| get_project_capabilities | Browse user-observable behaviors and acceptance criteria |
| get_data_flows | See how data moves across the system |
| get_project_rules | Check constraints before committing — ADRs, principles, invariants |
| get_tech_stack_overview | Languages, frameworks, external dependencies |
| get_project_state | Full current state overview (metadata + drill paths) |
| get_guidance | Best practices, production readiness, checklists |
| query_impact_graph | Code-level dependencies + blast radius |

Call `get_server_capabilities` to discover all available tools.

## When to lean on gjalla

- Orient before touching code — load `get_architecture_spec`, scan
  `get_project_rules`, optionally drill into elements
- Check rules before committing — `get_project_rules`
- Check production readiness before shipping —
  `get_guidance(intent="production_readiness")` and
  `get_guidance(intent="production_checklist")`
- Review your changes — `/gjalla-review` for spec/rules/ops compliance
- Project your master-spec delta — `/gjalla-impact`
- Attest on commit — `/gjalla-attest` (requires gjalla CLI for write)
